{
  "_comment": "Modifier chips: what the player reads on the result screen to reconstruct the roll (design pillar 2, legible randomness). NOT checked by content:lint — keysOf() walks event-derived keys only — so a missing one here ships a raw key to the screen rather than failing a build. There is a test in packages/content/__tests__ that covers the gap.",

  "_comment_kinds": "check.kind.<sourceKind>: the label a COLLAPSED chip takes when two or more rows of one sourceKind fold together — \"Condition x3, -4\". A chip of one keeps the row's own check.modifier.<id> label instead, so these only ever render for a fold. One per entry of MODIFIER_SOURCE_KINDS; the vocabulary is closed, so the set below is complete by construction. See docs/adr/0037.",

